<!-- Written verbatim inside <manifest> in AndroidManifest.xml by buildozer's
     android.extra_manifest_xml option.

     targetSdk is 34, and since Android 11 an app can only see the packages it
     declares an interest in.  Without this element the package manager hides
     Termux from us: resolveService() returns null, the RUN_COMMAND intent does
     nothing, and pressing DOWNLOAD would always fall back to the share sheet.
     github.com/termux/termux-app/wiki/Termux-Libraries#target-sdk-30-package-visibility

     Single-quoted attribute (valid XML): buildozer interpolates this file into
     a shell command wrapped in double quotes, without escaping anything, so a
     double quote here would end that string and split the argument. -->
<queries>
    <package android:name='com.termux' />
</queries>
